  "finalText": "I built the \"Boop!\" intro as a 6-second, 1080×1080 piece on a cream `#FFF4E6` background. The critic scores it 99/100.\n\n- **Candy drop (0–1.6 s):** six shapes fall in staggered 0.12 s apart: a coral circle, two sun-yellow stars, a green rounded square, a blue circle, a lilac star and a small sun circle. Each stretches on the way down, squashes on contact, and rebounds.\n- **Jostle (1.6–2.4 s):** each shape gets a quick sideways bump with a squash, one after another, then settles.\n- **Letters hop (2.5–4.2 s):** **B**, **o**, **o**, **p** and **!** drop onto the baseline one by one, 0.14 s apart. Each squashes on landing and bounces up. The **!** is coral and gets the biggest hop.\n- **Idle wiggle (4.6 s on):** all shapes and letters rock gently with out-of-phase rotation, so the final frame stays alive.\n\nChoices I made:\n- Letters are ink `#2B2D42`, with the **!** in a darker coral (`#D9364A`) so it passes contrast.\n- The lockup sits slightly high on the canvas, with empty space below the wordmark. I didn't move it; I can shift the whole lockup down if you want it centred.\n- No sound effects or music, since you didn't ask for them.\n\nWant the wiggle stronger, the bounces bouncier, or the lockup moved down?"
